reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T11","usage":{"input_tokens":7099,"output_tokens":602,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"56bfba63e3e265c013bbc8d6c1d38529f93cfb3403e9dd100fa0fa11f4586e95"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":25167,"output_tokens":1356,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"982f82010ffc1720207e4e316851057d4cc74913bd0724312f70b97bf99d4458"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:E4","usage":{"input_tokens":115759,"output_tokens":4286,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"171ac12526c7a0838599518d9cd1e701d8b1b4b2f91889ce558a13bf3516941d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":41829,"output_tokens":1630,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"e06ac102745256b8f2eb963aac624f81fd512286e0cdc43de1c1fb9b4b351285"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":40525,"output_tokens":2135,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"72fa8665820b1342dde298b31924807eb39e47b478c7b284b151c85f3edf678b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":56079,"output_tokens":3824,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive FsckOut's patch sites from the BridgeFsckOut reference graph and add the missing ones: mcp_server.py import block, mcp_server.py __all__, and the `except ImportError` None-fallback in _mcp_models.py.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.025,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 3: \"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py — add FsckOut ... following the _Out / ClarityResultOut / BridgeFsckOut pattern\"","mcp_server.py:40 imports BridgeFsckOut and mcp_server.py:68 lists it in __all__; comment at mcp_server.py:34-35: \"Re-exported here for back-compat: existing callers import e.g. rebar.mcp_server.NextBatchOut / ValidateReportOut directly.\"","_mcp_models.py:399 `BridgeFsckOut = None  # type: ignore` inside the `except ImportError` fallback — a peer-model site the plan's step 3 does not name","The plan enumerates only three patch sites for FsckOut and cites BridgeFsckOut as the template, but BridgeFsckOut resolves to five distinct edit sites."],"finding":"The new symbol FsckOut's patch-site inventory omits mcp_server.py, even though the plan explicitly follows the BridgeFsckOut pattern. Every peer _Out model (including BridgeFsckOut) is both imported in mcp_server.py's model import block and listed in its __all__; the file comment states these re-exports exist \"for back-compat: existing callers import e.g. rebar.mcp_server.NextBatchOut directly.\" Additionally, _mcp_models.py's except-ImportError block sets every _Out model (BridgeFsckOut at line 399) to None; FsckOut must be added there too or it is undefined when pydantic is absent — and _mcp_reads.py imports it at module top (line 24).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff551de411bdf1e6d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 3-5 (FsckOut in _mcp_models.py, _mcp_reads.py, check_mcp_models.MODEL_SCHEMAS)","norm_id":"n2d6a2b371d49a269","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["mcp_server.py import block (lines 37-58): FsckOut not added → any back-compat caller doing `from rebar.mcp_server import FsckOut` breaks, inconsistent with every peer model","mcp_server.py __all__ (lines 64-89): FsckOut absent → not re-exported, diverging from the BridgeFsckOut pattern the plan invokes","_mcp_models.py except-ImportError block (lines 391-405): FsckOut not set to None → when the mcp extra/pydantic is unavailable, `from rebar._mcp_models import ... FsckOut` at _mcp_reads.py:24 raises ImportError instead of degrading gracefully like every other _Out model"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In step 3, add FsckOut to both the class definition AND the `except ImportError` None-assignment block in _mcp_models.py; add a step covering mcp_server.py's model import block and __all__ so FsckOut is re-exported like BridgeFsckOut.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED counter modified in `_commands/fsck_scan.py` (step 6) is the same tally that drives the non-zero exit cited at `_commands/fsck.py:242-243`, and reconcile the file references.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Mechanism: 'src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:242-243 — the CLI exits non-zero when issue_count > 0'","Step 6: 'AC4 (src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py) — STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED stops incrementing the issue counter'","Table sources: '_commands/fsck.py:17-18,242-243'"],"finding":"The scan command's files are named inconsistently: the Mechanism section and the contract table cite `_commands/fsck.py` (issue_count/exit at fsck.py:242-243), while step 6's STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED change targets `_commands/fsck_scan.py`. The plan does not establish that the counter increment step 6 modifies is the same counter that drives the exit code cited in fsck.py.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f41c4405f25752d6d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 6 vs Mechanism section / contract table","norm_id":"n903db16191062b6d","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer edits fsck_scan.py's counter but the exit at fsck.py:242 reads a different tally, so STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED still influences the exit code, silently failing AC6."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line note in step 6 stating that fsck_scan.py's issue counter feeds fsck.py's exit decision (or name the single file that does both), so the implementer edits the counter that governs the exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_s